 # xurl — X (Twitter) API via the Official CLI
@@ -30,6 +43,28 @@ Use this skill for:
 
 This skill replaces the older `xitter` skill (which wrapped a third-party Python CLI). `xurl` is maintained by the X developer platform team, supports OAuth 2.0 PKCE with auto-refresh, and covers a substantially larger API surface.
 
+## When to Use
+
+Load this skill when the user wants to:
+- Post, reply to, quote, or delete posts on X/Twitter
+- Search posts, timelines, or mentions
+- Like, repost, bookmark, follow, or block users
+- Send or read direct messages
+- Upload images or videos
+- Check their X account status or lookup users
+- Use raw X API v2 endpoints
+- Manage multiple X apps or accounts
+- Troubleshoot xurl authentication issues
+
+## Not For
+
+- General web browsing or scraping → use `browser`, `web_search`, or `web_extract`
+- Third-party Twitter clients (TweetDeck, Hootsuite, etc.) → use their own APIs or UIs
+- Reading X without an account → unauthenticated access is heavily rate-limited; most queries need auth
+- Bulk data extraction or research → X API rate limits make this impractical for large datasets
+- Sentiment analysis or NLP on tweets → extract text first, then use ML tools separately
+- Managing other social platforms (Bluesky, Mastodon, LinkedIn) → use platform-specific tools
+
 ---
 
 ## Secret Safety (MANDATORY)
