+## Pitfalls
+
+1. **Auth errors after "successful" OAuth flow.** The #1 xurl setup mistake: running `xurl auth oauth2` without `--app my-app` saves tokens to the empty `default` profile. The fix is `xurl auth oauth2 --app my-app` then `xurl auth default my-app`.
+
+2. **Verbose mode leaks tokens.** Never use `-v` / `--verbose` in agent sessions — it prints auth headers to stdout, which enters the LLM context. The skill explicitly forbids this, but subagents or new skills may not know.
+
+3. **Media processing delays.** Video uploads need server-side processing before posting. A post with a fresh video upload may fail silently. Always check `xurl media status MEDIA_ID` and wait for `succeeded` before posting.
+
+4. **Rate limits on write endpoints.** Posting, liking, following have tight rate limits. A 429 doesn't mean the command was wrong — it means "wait." Implement retry with exponential backoff or space out write operations.
+
+5. **Multiple apps without defaults.** If the user has 2+ apps registered but no default set, commands may use the wrong credentials. Always verify with `xurl auth status` which app has the `▸` marker.
+
+6. **Wrong redirect URI.** The OAuth callback must be exactly `http://localhost:8080/callback`. A trailing slash or different port breaks the PKCE flow. Dashboard → User Authentication Settings → Callback URL.
+
+7. **`UsernameNotFound` after OAuth.** X's `/2/users/me` endpoint is flaky for some accounts. Fix: pass the username explicitly during OAuth: `xurl auth oauth2 --app my-app YOUR_USERNAME`.
+
+8. **Posting without confirming intent.** Write actions (post, reply, like, DM, follow, block) are destructive or public. Always confirm the exact text/target with the user before executing.
+
+9. **Using full tweet URLs as post IDs.** `xurl read https://x.com/user/status/1234567890` works, but `xurl reply https://...` may not. Extract the numeric ID from the URL for write operations.
+
+10. **Forgetting `--app` on per-request overrides.** `xurl --app staging /2/users/me` works for one-off calls, but `xurl post "test"` with `--app staging` may fail if staging has no default user set.
+
